<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-santomea-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila santomea Schnakenberg wavelength at 2.326 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma), pass 2 — MorphoEval overall 86.7/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the pass-1 dispersion identity (RMSE 4.9e-5) and adds the four remediations. Across γ in {0.70, 1, 1.287, 1.598, 2.10} the analytic wavelength decreases monotonically and the numeric-peak wavelength tracks it with Pearson r = 0.984 (RMSE 0.91 µm; the discrete peak sits long of k_c). Equal diffusion gives σ(k_c) = -0.451 against wild-type σ = +0.285. The gallery bar is 110 px = 100 µm (0.909 µm/px); the radial peak is 90.909 µm, 39.1 times 2.326 µm. Two-sample KS between gallery luminance and the activator is 0.249. GIF remains 12 frames at 800×600. Overall 86.7/100 (faithfulness 85.9, reproducibility 88.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_santomea_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-santomea-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 506876 B, 1248×960 px, artifact_sha256 c0f9011955e25636bbf84acbbdb74e4fe2c036ce9049b3d29716c09b56a4cec5 (sha256 c0f9011955e25636bbf84acbbdb74e4fe2c036ce9049b3d29716c09b56a4cec5), spec_fingerprint 6dd554cc130d1b0176b37753cfbd7be017befc53ffb878bd36cf5f79710bf34c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 6dd554cc130d1b0176b37753cfbd7be017befc53ffb878bd36cf5f79710bf34c; artifact_sha256: c0f9011955e25636bbf84acbbdb74e4fe2c036ce9049b3d29716c09b56a4cec5; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_santomea_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_santomea_specimen.jpg=9ea05ad5963c10d3..., datasets/drosophila_santomea_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_santomea_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=f16b54dd44acea38..., datasets/drosophila_santomea_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=fb23a9fc5fb610db...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-santomea-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 gives k_c from the linearized reaction-diffusion Jacobian. | Schnakenberg 1979 supplies the kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v. | Jeong et al. 2008 show loss of abdominal tan expression in D. santomea relative to D. yakuba.; reconstructed_in_script: ξ is chosen so γ = 1 yields λ_c = 2.326 µm on this Jacobian. | Predecessor D. pseudoobscura is assigned 1.840 µm and successor D. sechellia 2.050 µm at this same tier, with γ ∝ 1/λ^2. | The gallery radial peak is converted with the drawn 100 µm bar.; transfer_boundary: Neighbor wavelengths belong to the 2.3 µm tier only. They are not the 88 µm and 114 µm primordium slots.; does_not_claim: That Jeong, Llopart, or Lachaise measured 2.326 µm. | That D. pseudoobscura is the ancestor of D. santomea. The sister species is D. yakuba. | That the gallery arm spacing of 90.909 µm confirms the model wavelength. It contradicts a literal reading of the image as a 2.3 µm micrograph. | That a second, independent assessor model scored this audit.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: A second assessor from another model family has not scored this audit.",
        "remediation needed: Replace the gallery spiral with a CC micrograph that actually resolves cuticle pigment near 2 µm; the present radial peak is 90.909 µm.",
        "remediation needed: The numeric wavelength peak is biased long (sweep RMSE 0.91 µm) even though rank agreement is 0.984. A finer k grid would tighten it." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.67e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-santomea-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila santomea Schnakenberg wavelength at 2.326 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma), pass 2 — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Five γ values produce a strictly decreasing analytic wavelength, and the numeric peak moves the same way (r = 0.984). Equal diffusion is the negative control on D_v/D_u. Chronoseries γ values are the two interior sweep points 1.287 and 1.598." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-santomea-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-santomea-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

