    pk:hasScore 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-santomea-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila santomea Schnakenberg wavelength at 2.326 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma), pass 2 (Drosophila santomea)",
        "Drosophila santomea Schnakenberg wavelength at 2.326 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma), pass 2 faithfully reproduces Drosophila santomea morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-santomea-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-santomea-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-santomea-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-santomea-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila santomea specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-santomea-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila santomea" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That D. pseudoobscura is the ancestor of D. santomea. The sister species is D. yakuba.",
        "does_not_claim: That Jeong, Llopart, or Lachaise measured 2.326 µm.",
        "does_not_claim: That a second, independent assessor model scored this audit.",
        "does_not_claim: That the gallery arm spacing of 90.909 µm confirms the model wavelength. It contradicts a literal reading of the image as a 2.3 µm micrograph.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Predecessor D. pseudoobscura is assigned 1.840 µm and successor D. sechellia 2.050 µm at this same tier, with γ ∝ 1/λ^2.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: The gallery radial peak is converted with the drawn 100 µm bar.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: ξ is chosen so γ = 1 yields λ_c = 2.326 µm on this Jacobian.",
        "reported_in_source: Jeong et al. 2008 show loss of abdominal tan expression in D. santomea relative to D. yakuba.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 supplies the kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 gives k_c from the linearized reaction-diffusion Jacobian.",
        "transfer_boundary: Neighbor wavelengths belong to the 2.3 µm tier only. They are not the 88 µm and 114 µm primordium slots." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila santomea (São Tomé Highland Mist-Forest Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-santomea-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_santomea_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila santomea; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 gives k_c from the linearized reaction-diffusion Jacobian. | Schnakenberg 1979 supplies the kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v. | Jeong et al. 2008 show loss of abdominal tan expression in D. santomea relative to D. yakuba.; reconstructed_in_script: ξ is chosen so γ = 1 yields λ_c = 2.326 µm on this Jacobian. | Predecessor D. pseudoobscura is assigned 1.840 µm and successor D. sechellia 2.050 µm at this same tier, with γ ∝ 1/λ^2. | The gallery radial peak is converted with the drawn 100 µm bar.; transfer_boundary: Neighbor wavelengths belong to the 2.3 µm tier only. They are not the 88 µm and 114 µm primordium slots.; does_not_claim: That Jeong, Llopart, or Lachaise measured 2.326 µm. | That D. pseudoobscura is the ancestor of D. santomea. The sister species is D. yakuba. | That the gallery arm spacing of 90.909 µm confirms the model wavelength. It contradicts a literal reading of the image as a 2.3 µm micrograph. | That a second, independent assessor model scored this audit.]; other sources: Simple chemical reaction systems with limit cycle behaviour <https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/0022519379902580>; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2008.01.014>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2000.1169>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.0014-3820.2002.tb00150.x> ;
    pk:externalAtlasDataset <https://codex.flywire.ai/>,
        <https://flybase.org/>,
        <https://flycellatlas.org/>,
        <https://insitu.fruitfly.org/>,
        <https://www.virtualflybrain.org/> ;
    pk:fossilLineageGroup "Sophophora melanogaster Subgroup Radiation (0–12 Ma)" ;
